I wonder if [this case](https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/blob/80a5f3ac0d1eac8f22f6cdbca6e3c2e3f2f6939e/server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/engine/InternalEngine.java#L977):

```
            plan = IndexingStrategy.processButSkipLucene(false, index.version());
```

combined with the [check in `index`](https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/blob/80a5f3ac0d1eac8f22f6cdbca6e3c2e3f2f6939e/server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/engine/InternalEngine.java#L896):

```
                        final boolean toAppend = plan.indexIntoLucene && plan.useLuceneUpdateDocument == false;
                        if (toAppend == false) {
                            advanceMaxSeqNoOfUpdatesOrDeletesOnPrimary(index.seqNo());
                        }
```

could lead to this assertion firing. The check in `index` is slightly lenient in that it says to `advance` even if not indexing the document at all. In the non-indexing case it is fine on primary/leader to update the max seq-no (is a conservative estimate anyway), but the assertion on follower will fail.
